.TH UWCCCTL 1 "October 2026" "open-uniwill-cc 1.6.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
uwccctl \- command line control for open-uniwill-cc (Uniwill laptops)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B uwccctl
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.br
.B uwccctl help
.RI [ command ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B uwccctl
controls the
.B uwccd
service: performance modes and profiles, fan tables, battery protection, keyboard
and light bar backlight, switches, automation, the Bluetooth liquid cooler, history,
backups and diagnostic reports.
Everything the window can change is available here, so the laptop can be managed
from scripts, hotkeys, SSH or a system without a desktop.
.PP
The tool talks to the service on 127.0.0.1 with the token in
.IR /run/uwcc/token ,
which is readable by the
.B uwcc
group (the installer adds the user to it; log out and in once after installation) and by root.
Commands without arguments print the current state; commands with arguments change it
and then print the new state.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print the result as JSON (one document;
.B monitor \-\-watch
prints one JSON object per line).
Errors become
.B {"error": "..."}
on standard output.
The option may stand anywhere on the command line.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Overview; after a command \(em help for that command.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Overview
.TP
.B status
Laptop model, mode and profile, PL limits, fans, temperatures, battery, liquid cooler and switches.
With
.B \-\-json
prints
.B {"state": ..., "monitor": ...}
as the service reports them.
.TP
.BR "monitor " [ \-\-watch " [" \fISEC\fR ]]
CPU and GPU temperature, load, clock and power, fan speeds, memory, battery.
.B \-\-watch
repeats every
.I SEC
seconds (default 2, at least 0.5) until Ctrl+C.
.TP
.BR "history " [ csv | csv\-excel | json "] [" 1m | 5m | 15m | 1h | 24h "] [" \fIFILE\fR ]
Recorded sensor history (default: csv, 1h; json with
.BR \-\-json )
to standard output or
.IR FILE .
.SS Performance
.TP
.BR "mode " [ office | gaming | turbo | custom ]
Show or switch the performance mode.
.B custom
exists on platforms with RamFan 1.5 and five custom slots.
.TP
.BR "profile " [\fIN\fR]
Show the active profile, or select slot
.I N
(counted from 0) of the current mode.
.TP
.B profile list
All profiles; the active one is marked with *.
.TP
.BR "profile show " [\fITARGET\fR]
Values of a profile.
.TP
.BR "profile set " [\fITARGET\fR] " \fIKEY\fR=\fIVALUE\fR ..."
Change a profile. Keys:
.RS
.TP 10
.BR pl1 ", " pl2 ", " pl4
CPU power limits, W (PL2 is raised to PL1; PL4 must not be lower than PL2).
.TP
.B tcc
TCC offset, \(deC below Tjmax, or
.BR off .
.TP
.B ctgp
Configurable TGP of the NVIDIA GPU, W, or
.BR off .
.TP
.B db
Dynamic Boost, W, or
.BR off .
.TP
.B gputemp
GPU temperature limit, \(deC, or
.BR off .
.TP
.B fanspeed
Fan switch speed, rpm (100..12700), or
.BR off .
.TP
.B name
Name of a custom slot (up to 24 characters).
.RE
.IP
The service checks the ranges of this laptop and reports a violated one as an error.
.TP
.BR "profile reset " [\fITARGET\fR]
Factory values and the factory fan curve of the slot.
.PP
.I TARGET
is a mode
.RB ( office ),
a mode and a slot counted from 0
.RB ( custom:2 ),
or a raw profile name
.RB ( Mode4_Profile3 ).
Without it the active profile is used.
.TP
.BR "boost " [ on | off ]
FanBoost: both fans at maximum speed.
.TP
.BR "super " [ on | off ]
Super performance: Turbo fan table, maximum cTGP and Dynamic Boost, independent of the mode.
.TP
.BR "ramoc " [ on | off ]
RAM overclocking (BIOS variable MemoryOverClockSwitch).
Takes effect after a reboot; reported as pending until then.
.TP
.B restore \-\-yes
Factory profiles and fan tables of every mode.
.SS Fan tables
.TP
.B fan list
Tables and the profiles that use them; the active table is marked with *.
.TP
.BR "fan show " [\fITABLE\fR]
Levels of a table as
.IR UP / DOWN : DUTY .
.TP
.BI "fan set " "TABLE " cpu | gpu " POINT ..."
Replace the curve. A point is
.IR UP / DOWN : DUTY
\(em the temperature at which the level starts, the temperature at which the fan drops
back to the previous level, and the fan speed in percent.
Up to 16 levels; level 0 starts at 0 \(deC, temperatures must not decrease and the highest
level must run the fan at 40 % or more.
.TP
.BI "fan set " "TABLE " "\-\-file " FILE
Load a table saved with
.BR "fan show \-\-json" .
.TP
.BI "fan separate " "TABLE " on | off
Separate CPU and GPU curves (FanControlRespective).
.TP
.BI "fan reset " TABLE
Factory curve.
.PP
.I TABLE
is a name from
.B fan list
(M1T1 .. M4T5) or
.BR current .
.SS Battery
.TP
.B battery
Protection mode, charge limits, cycles, Type\-C priority.
.TP
.BR "battery mode " full | balanced | stationary
Battery protection mode.
.TP
.BI "battery limit " UP " \fR[\fIDOWN\fR]"
Stop charging at
.I UP
% (1..100) and resume below
.I DOWN
% (1..95).
.TP
.BR "battery typec " on | off
Charge from the Type\-C adapter first.
.SS Keyboard and light bar
.TP
.B kb
Backlight state, current effect and the keyboard controller.
.TP
.BR "kb " on | off
.TP
.B kb effects
Effects with their numbers; unsupported ones are marked, and so are effects drawn by
the service (they need the service running).
.TP
.BI "kb effect " NAME | N " \fR[\fIoptions\fR]"
Start an effect. Options not given keep their current values:
.RS
.TP 22
.BI \-\-light " 0..4"
brightness
.TP
.BI \-\-speed " 0..4"
speed
.TP
.BR \-\-dir " right|left|up|down"
direction
.TP
.BI \-\-color " RRGGBB\fR[,\fIRRGGBB\fR...]"
colour or palette
.TP
.BR \-\-multi ", " \-\-no\-multi
multicolour (circular palette)
.TP
.BI \-\-text " TEXT"
text of the Alphabet effect
.RE
.TP
.BI "kb feedback " NAME " yes" | no
Did an untested effect (applied with \fB\-\-try\fR) work? Kept for the diagnostic report.
.TP
.BI "kb level " N
Brightness 0..4.
.TP
.B kb fx
BetterRGB effects (drawn by the service frame by frame): numbers, parameters and the engine settings.
.TP
.BI "kb fx " NAME | N " \fR[\fB\-\-light \fI0..4\fR] [\fIKEY\fB=\fIVALUE\fR ...]"
Start a BetterRGB effect. Colours as \fBcolors=\fIRRGGBB\fB,\fIRRGGBB\fR, switches as \fBon\fR|\fBoff\fR.
.TP
.BI "kb fx\-config " KEY = VALUE " ..."
\fBfps_ac\fR, \fBfps_battery\fR (10..60), \fBtransition\fR, \fBtransition_ms\fR, \fBbar\fR
(off|battery|volume|mic|cpu|gpu|audio), \fBbar_direction\fR, \fBbar_start\fR, \fBbar_end\fR.
.TP
.BR "kb fx\-calibrate " start | cancel | reset ", " "kb fx\-calibrate apply \fIRRGGBB"
White calibration: the keys show raw white, \fIRRGGBB\fR is the colour you see.
.TP
.BR "lb " [ hinge | base | logo "] " on | off
.TP
.BI "lb \fR[\fIZONE\fR] color " RRGGBB " \fR[\fIEFFECT\fR]"
.TP
.BR "lb " [\fIZONE\fR] " effect " static | breathing | breathing_multi | wave | cycle | rainbow | colorbreath | colorwave
.TP
.BI "lb \fR[\fIZONE\fR] light " 0..4
Light bar zones; the default zone is
.BR hinge .
.TP
.B lighting
Keyboard and light bar devices (diagnostics).
.SS Automatic profile switching
.TP
.BR "rules " [ list ]
Rules that switch the mode and profile by power, temperature or load, and their state.
.TP
.BI "rules export " FILE ", rules import " FILE
The rules as JSON; import replaces them (see
.BR "uwccctl help rules" ).
.TP
.BR "rules enable " N ", " "rules disable " N ", " "rules clear"
.TP
.BI "lc pump-limits " "7,8,11,12 " "\-\-accept\-risks" "\fR | \fBoff"
Own pump voltages (the cooler knows only 7, 8, 11 and 12 V).
.SS Control Center 3.0 / Clevo (experimental)
Separate module for laptops with Control Center 3.x (Clevo "DCHU" interface); see docs/CLEVO.md.
Commands are refused until
.B clevo writes on
is set.
.TP
.B clevo
Interface, capabilities, fans and the settings last set here (the firmware does not report them).
.TP
.BR "clevo writes" | restore " " on | off
Allow commands; send the saved settings again when the service starts.
.TP
.BR "clevo power " quiet | powersave | performance | entertainment
.TP
.BR "clevo fan " auto | max | maxq | custom
.TP
.BI "clevo fan offset " 0..100
.TP
.BI "clevo fan curve " "FAN T,D T,D T,D"
Custom curve of
.BR cpu ", " gpu1 " or " gpu2
(the first point stays the factory one), then custom mode.
.TP
.BR "clevo fan defaults" ", " "clevo antidust"
Factory fan curve; anti-dust cycle.
.TP
.BR "clevo kb " on | off
.TP
.BI "clevo kb color " RRGGBB " \fR[\fIZONE\fR]"
.TP
.BI "clevo kb brightness " 0..255
.TP
.BR "clevo kb effect " random | breathe | cycle | wave | dance | tempo | flash
.TP
.BI "clevo kb sleep " SECONDS
.TP
.BR "clevo kb boot\-effect " on | off
.SS Switches and automation
.TP
.BR "get " [\fIKEY\fR]
All switches and automation settings, or one of them.
.TP
.BI "set " "KEY VALUE"
Change one. Boolean values:
.BR on / off .
.RS
.TP 20
.B Switches
winkey_lock, fn_lock, usb_charger, touchpad_toggle, touchpad_enabled, ac_recovery,
dgpu_direct, bluetooth, wifi, webcam, osd, lc_hwoc, kb_picture_modes, tcc_extended,
history_record, update_check, debug, mem_oc, super_performance
.TP
.B kb_timeout
keyboard backlight timeout, s (0..3600, 0 = never)
.TP
.B Automation
alerts, overheat_boost, kb_off_on_battery, ppd_sync (on/off);
cpu_alert, gpu_alert (60..105 \(deC);
mode_on_ac
.RB ( keep | previous |\fImode\fR),
mode_on_battery
.RB ( keep |\fImode\fR)
.TP
.B lightbar_trigger
toggle the light bar as the hotkey does
.TP
.B lang
.BR en | ru
.TP
.B fan_manager
.BR auto " (by project), " cml ", " std ;
the service restarts
.RE
.TP
.B apps
Rules that switch the mode while a program runs.
.TP
.BI "apps add " "PROCESS MODE"
For example
.BR "apps add steam gaming" .
.TP
.BI "apps remove " PROCESS
.TP
.BR "apps enable" | disable " \fIPROCESS\fR"
.SS Liquid cooler
.TP
.BR "lc " [ status ]
.TP
.B lc scan
Find coolers nearby.
.TP
.BI "lc connect " ADDR
Connect and remember; the service reconnects automatically.
.TP
.BR "lc disconnect " [ \-\-forget ]
.TP
.BR "lc mode " auto | laptop | ec | manual | high | medium | low | off
.TP
.BI "lc manual " "FAN PUMP"
Fan 0..100 %, pump 7, 8, 11 or 12 V (0 = off).
.TP
.BR "lc curve " [ common | office | gaming | turbo | custom ]
Show the curves: common (Automatic, and Follow the laptop for modes without their own) and per laptop mode.
.TP
.BI "lc curve " "KEY " "fan " T:D " ... [pump " T:V " ...]"
Set a curve: fan 2..17 points, pump 1..4 steps of 7, 8 or 11 V; a first step of 0 V keeps the pump off below the next one.
.TP
.BI "lc curve " "KEY " "flat " "FAN \fR[\fIPUMP\fR]"
A flat curve;
.BI "lc curve " "MODE " off
makes the mode use the common curve.
.TP
.BR "lc profile " [ list | apply | save | copy | remove | rename ]
Cooler profiles: quiet, balanced, performance and your own.
.TP
.BI "lc tiers " BELOW : FAN : PUMP " ..."
The tier form of 1.6.7; becomes the common curve.
.TP
.BI "lc set " "KEY VALUE"
.B temp_source
.RB ( max | cpu | gpu ),
.BR delay_up ", " delay_down
(0..300 s),
.BR smooth ", " notify_flow ", " flow_guard ", " boost_fan ", " boost_pump
.RB ( on / off ).
.TP
.BR "lc idle " on | off " [\fIKEY\fR=\fIVALUE\fR ...]"
Stop the pump at low temperature: off_below, off_after, on_above, on_after, min_run.
.TP
\fBlc rgb\fR \fIRRGGBB\fR [\fIMODE\fR] | \fBlc rgb off\fR
Modes: static, breathe, rainbow, breathe_rainbow, spiral, rotating_rainbow, color_wave.
.TP
.BR "lc prime " [ stop ]
Coolant filling cycle (about 68 s).
.TP
.B lc suspend
Put the cooler to sleep (used by the system\-sleep hook).
.SS Service
.TP
.BR "export fans" | all " [\fIFILE\fR]"
Fan tables, or a full backup with profiles, settings and the liquid cooler.
.TP
.BI "import " FILE " \fR[fans,profiles,settings] [\-\-force]"
Default sections: fans,profiles.
.B \-\-force
accepts a backup of another laptop model.
.TP
.BI "report \fR[\fIFILE\fR] [\-\-private " LIST "\fR] [\-\-sections " LIST "\fR] [\-\-full]"
Diagnostic zip for bug reports.
.B \-\-private
hides serial, uuid, mac, names, apps.
.TP
.BR "lang " en | ru
Language of the window, notifications and this tool.
.TP
.BR "debug " [ on | off ]
Verbose service log.
.TP
.B version
.TP
.BR "update " [ check | install ]
Check GitHub for a new release; install works on Windows only.
.TP
.B restart
Restart the service (members of uwcc may do it through polkit).
.TP
.B resume
Re\-apply the settings (used after sleep).
.TP
.BI "ec read " ADDR
Read an EC register (hex) through the service.
.TP
.B nvram
UniWillVariable fields.
.TP
.BR "driver " [ use " " auto | oem | wmi " [" \-\-accept\-risks ]]
Windows: how the service reaches the EC.
.B auto
\(em the OEM driver UWACPIDriver, WMI only when it is missing and the warning was accepted (default);
.B oem
\(em the OEM driver only;
.B wmi
\(em the Windows built\-in WMI only: open implementation, not recommended, beta (no liquid\-cooling power boost,
approximate limits, about 125 ms per EC access; tested only on MAIBENBEN Tsunami X629 / Mechrevo Questyle 16 Super /
XMG NEO 16 (E23)).
.TP
.BR "driver config export" | import " \fIFILE\fR" | reset ", " "driver test"
WMI settings
.IR ec_wmi.json ,
quick test of the active path. See docs/EC/WMI\-config.md.
Changing the path, the WMI settings and the platform profile needs administrator rights.
.B uwccctl ec
is the same command (EC Manager).
.TP
.BR "driver unlock " [\fIMIN\fR] " | " lock
Open the EC Manager settings for the window for MIN minutes (default 10). Needs administrator rights (Windows) or
root (sudo): the command reads the administrator key of the service.
.TP
.BR "driver monitor " oem | wmi | all " " on | off
Monitoring through this EC path. Off for a path: temperatures only, every 20 s (liquid cooler, overheat alerts);
all off: nothing is read, the liquid cooler in the automatic mode runs the Medium preset.
.TP
.BR "driver platform " [ export | import " \fIFILE\fR | " reset | apply\-draft ]
Platform profile of this laptop: which functions work through WMI, limits, tested versions. See docs/EC/Platforms.md.
.TP
.BR "driver selfcheck " [ 1 | 2 "] [\-\-export \fIFILE\fR]"
Self\-check: 1 reads only; 2 also switches functions briefly and back with read\-back (administrator, AC power).
Prints what works and what is not clear; \-\-export writes the result and a draft platform profile for GitHub.
.TP
\fBec\-direct read\fR \fIADDR\fR [\fIN\fR] | \fBec\-direct dump\fR \fIBASE\fR
Read the EC without the service (root).
.TP
.B release
Give fan control back to the EC and clear the program's BIOS flags (root; used by uninstall).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
The service rejected the request (value out of range, feature not available on this laptop).
.TP
.B 2
Wrong usage.
.TP
.B 3
The service is not running or access is denied.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B UWCC_PORT
Service port (default 47321).
.TP
.B UWCC_TOKEN
Use this token instead of reading the token file.
.TP
.B UWCC_TOKEN_FILE
Path of the token file (default
.IR /run/uwcc/token ).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /run/uwcc/token
Access token of the running service.
.TP
.I /var/lib/uwcc
Settings, profiles, fan tables and history.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
uwccctl mode turbo
uwccctl profile set custom:0 pl1=65 pl2=90 tcc=10 ctgp=off name=Quiet
uwccctl fan set current cpu 0/45:0 55/50:30 70/65:60 85/80:100
uwccctl battery limit 80 60
uwccctl kb effect wave \-\-speed 3 \-\-multi
uwccctl kb effect single \-\-color 00A0FF \-\-light 2
uwccctl set mode_on_battery office
uwccctl apps add steam gaming
uwccctl \-\-json monitor | jq .cpu.temp
uwccctl \-\-json monitor \-\-watch 5 >> sensors.ndjson
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR journalctl (1)
.PP
https://github.com/aspidovss/open-uniwill-cc
.SH NOTES
On Windows the same commands are available in
.BR uwccctl.exe ;
use
.B uwccctl help
.I command
instead of this page.
